      <div type="clause" n="74.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 74.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="74.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="120" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> þone ceap<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.26"/> nelle foregesellan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.27"/>, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> mot hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.28"/> se hlaford gefreogean<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.29"/>; gielden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.30"/> siððan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.31"/> his mægas þone wer, gif he mægburg<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.32"/> hæbbe freo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.33"/>; gif he næbbe, heden his þa gefan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="74.1" corresp="#wit-ot-frags"><pb n="120" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he .....p nelle foregesel::n, þonne mot..; ..en siþþan his m..., ...æbbe freo; gif he ....</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="74.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="120" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he ðonne þone ceap nylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.3-2"/> foregesyllan, þonne mot hine se hlaford gefreogean<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.11"/>; gildon siððan his magas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.12"/> þone wer, gif he mægburh hæbbe freo; gif he næbbe, heden his ðonne ða gefan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="74.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="121" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf he ðonne ceap nelle foresyllan, þ[onne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.3"/>] mot hine se hlaford gefreogan; gyldan syððan his magas ðone wer, gyf he mægborh hæbbe freo; gyf he næbbe, heden his ða gefán.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="74.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="121" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.14"/> hoc captale nolit pro eo dare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.15"/>, tunc dominus eius liberum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.16"/> faciat eum; et soluant postea<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.17"/> parentes eius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.18"/> weram illam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.19"/> (occisi)<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.20"/>, si cognationem habeat liberam; si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.21"/> non habeat, obseruent eum inimici sui.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="60" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif he þonne þone<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_74-1.attnote.fn.2"/> ceap nelle foregesellan<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Ine_74-1.attnote.fn.3"/>, þonne mot hine se hlaford gefreogean; gielden siððan his mægas þone wer, gif he mægburg<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Ine_74-1.attnote.fn.4"/> hæbbe freo; gif he næbbe, heden his þa<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Ine_74-1.attnote.fn.5"/> gefan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="75.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="434" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif he þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> þone ceap nelle fore gesellan, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> mot hine se hlaford gefreogean. Gieldan siððan his mægas þone wer, gif he mægburg hæbbe freo. Gif he næbbe, heden his þa gefan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="121" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn er jedoch diesen Preis nicht für [ihn] hergeben will, dann darf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.de.1"/> ihn der Herr freigeben; es sollen alsdann seine [des Todtschlägers] Verwandte [für ihn] das Wergeld [des Erschlagenen an dessen Sippe] zahlen, falls<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.de.2"/> jener freie Verwandtschaft<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.de.3"/> besitzt; wenn er solche nicht besitzt, mögen sich die Rächer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.de.4"/> seiner<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_74-1.lnote.de.5"/> bemächtigen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But if he will not pay this price for [him], then the lord may set him free; his [the killer’s] kinsmen are then to pay the wergeld [of the slain man to his kin, for him], if he has free kindred; if he has none, let the avengers take hold of him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="61" ed="#attenborough"/>If, however, the lord will not pay this price for him, he must liberate him; afterwards his kinsmen must pay the wergeld, if he has a free kindred; if he has not [a free kindred], then his enemies may deal with him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="407" ed="#whitelock"/>If, however, he will not pay the price for him, the master must then set him free; his kinsmen are then to pay the wergild if he has a free kindred; if he has not, the avengers are to deal with him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="435" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If, however, he does not wish to pay this amount for him, then the lord may free him. His kinsmen must afterwards pay the <hi rend="italic">wer</hi> [for the slain man], if he has free kin. If he does not, then his enemies may take possession of him.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">121</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ꝥ, <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jahrh. dahinter:</hi> onne</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ꝥ, followed in the 16th cent. by: onne</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">121</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">diese Stellung Lond;</hi> Si do. ei. no. hoc ca. pro eo dare, li. <hi rend="italic">übrige ohne</hi> tunc</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">this word order Lond; Si do. ei. no. hoc ca. pro eo dare, li. the others, without tunc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">121</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">reddere <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">reddere MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">121</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">debet</hi> aut <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> li. f. e. et <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">debet</hi> aut instead of li. f. e. et K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">121</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">aus R Hn</hi> 70, 5; <hi rend="italic">fehlt LondTMHkBr;</hi> postea — nisi uelit <hi rend="italic">überspringt Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">from R Hn 70, 5; lacking in LondTMHkBr; Or skips postea — nisi uelit</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">121</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">illius <hi rend="italic">R T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">illius R T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">121</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> il. <hi rend="italic">Lond.; nur</hi> oc. <hi rend="italic">übrige;</hi> illam — liberam <hi rend="italic">theilweise ausradiert, am Rande:</hi> liberum faciat eum et so. oc., si co. ha. li.; si n. h., o. e. i. sui <hi rend="italic">Co</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only il. Lond.; only oc. the others; illam — liberam partly erased, in the margin: liberum faciat eum et so. oc., si co. ha. li.; si n. h., o. e. i. sui Co</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">121</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">hier</hi> postea <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">postea here Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">121</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">si — ini. sui <hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">si — ini. sui lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">zweites</hi> e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">second e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">erstes</hi> a <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">first a on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ceape <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ceape So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-syl. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-syl. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">se hl. hine <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">se hl. hine So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gyldan <hi rend="italic">Ld;</hi> ⁊ gyldan <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gyldan Ld; ⁊ gyldan So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syð. his magas þ. were <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syð. his magas þ. were So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">magborg <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> mægborh <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">magborg So; mægborh Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Schärfer fordert Preisgebung Hl 1. 3; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Haftung 6. Mit blossem Entäusserungsakt des Herrn begnügen sich auch andere Germanen; Brunner <hi rend="italic">Forsch. GDR</hi> 509</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hl 1. 3 demands surrender more strictly; <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> Haftung 6. Other Germanic peoples too are content with a mere act of relinquishment by the master; Brunner <hi rend="italic">Forsch. GDR</hi> 509</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das Band der Sippe (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 13 e. 24—26) tritt beim Strafhörigen durch die Freilassung (<hi rend="italic">s. d.</hi> 10 a) wieder in Kraft (<hi rend="italic">s.</hi> unfrei 9 c) und kann beim unfrei Geborenen von Einer, der freien Seite der Eltern her bestehen; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Af 27. Die Sippe ist die Blutrache (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 11) dem Genossen abkaufen zu helfen verpflichtet</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The bond of kinship (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 13 e. 24—26) comes back into force for the penal slave through manumission (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word 10 a) (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> unfrei 9 c), and in the case of a man born unfree it can exist through one side of the parents, the free side; <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> Af 27. The kindred is obliged to help its fellow-member buy off the blood-feud (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 11)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Über die falsche Variante <hi rend="italic">mægborg s. Wb: borg</hi> zu Ende</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On the false variant <hi rend="italic">mægborg see Wb: borg</hi> at the end</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hier <hi rend="spaced">kann</hi> die Freigebung zu Tötung (oder Verknechtung) des Totschlägers führen, die bei Preisgebung sicher scheint</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Here the release <hi rend="italic">can</hi> lead to the slayer’s being killed (or enslaved), which seems certain where he is surrendered</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_74-1.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘auf ihn fahnden’ (dies meint wohl Q), nicht ‘mögen sich vor ihm hüten’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘hunt for him’ (this is probably what Q means), not ‘may beware of him’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_74-1.attnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><label>þonne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">om. B.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 2 is printed 2 times on the page (74.1, 75), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_74-1.attnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><label>foregesellan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">foresyllan</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_74-1.attnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><label>mægburg</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">mægborh</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_74-1.attnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><label>þa</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ðonne ða</hi>. H.</seg></note>
